    "created_at": "2016-05-12T13:25:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-12T13:25:56Z",
    "body": "We don't need to do anything for Location.\n\nGiven the existence of `importScripts` and the fact that it loads cross-origin stuff, seems like we do want this for workers.  Certainly Gecko implements it for workers.\n\nI agree that this needs to be done in IDL, since IDL is what defines all the objects involved.\n\n@domenic The global needs to have a prototype that can't change.  Whether that's done via changing Window or WindowProxy is really an implementation detail.  But note that the immutable prototype thing also needs to apply to everthing on the global's proto chain: `Window.prototype`, the named properties object, `EventTarget.prototype`, and `Object.prototype`.  That last one already handled in ES; see https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/2016/#sec-properties-of-the-object-prototype-object.  Similarly, for workers, we need to apply this to `WorkerGlobalScope.prototype`, `DedicatedWorkerGlobalScope.prototype`, etc.\n\nIn terms of spec-wordsmithing, probably just explicitly say this for the named properties object, and for interface prototype objects say they're immutable-prototype if there is a [Global] or [PrimaryGlobal] interface that inherits from the given interface.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
